==============================================================================
G3. b=a+1, k=3 counterexample family: closed form check
==============================================================================
  a   b       N   x=ab^2+1   z=a^2 b  chi(x)  chi(1)  chi(z)   N-ab+1  in range
  2   3      24         19        12       2       2       2       19      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  3   4      60         49        36       2       2       2       49      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  4   5     120        101        80       2       2       2      101      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  5   6     210        181       150       2       2       2      181      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  6   7     336        295       252       2       2       2      295      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  7   8     504        449       392       2       2       2      449      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  8   9     720        649       576       2       2       2      649      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
  9  10     990        901       810       2       2       2      901      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
 10  11    1320       1211      1100       2       2       2     1211      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True
 11  12    1716       1585      1452       2       2       2     1585      True   eq=True mono=True  x==N-ab+1? True

  closed forms with b=a+1, k=3:
    N        = 2ab + a^2 b = a(a+1)(a+2) = a^3+3a^2+2a
    x        = a b^2 + 1   = a(a+1)^2+1  = a^3+2a^2+a+1
    N-ab+1   = a^3+3a^2+2a - a^2-a + 1   = a^3+2a^2+a+1   == x   <-- x is
               EXACTLY the left endpoint of the right-hand shell
    (asserted for a=2..11: all three closed forms exact)

==============================================================================
G4. k=2 case analysis -- which conjuncts does the refutation need?
==============================================================================

  k=2:  L_2 = a*b,  N = a*b,  no shell strata (range 2..k-1 empty).
        chi(j) = 1  iff  a | j  and  a^2 does not divide j     (v(j)=1)
        chi(j) = 2  otherwise                     (units, and v(j)>=2)

  A monochromatic solution needs y>=1, t>=1, x=y+bt<=N, z=at<=N.
  z = a*t <= a*b  and a>0  =>  t <= b.  With b < a:  1 <= t <= b < a.

  CASE 2 (all colour 2). The z-conjunct is  NOT(a|z AND a^2 not| z).
        a|z holds (z=at), so it forces a^2 | z, i.e. t = a*q for some q.
        1 <= t = a*q and a >= 2  =>  q >= 1  =>  t = a*q >= a > b >= t.
        CONTRADICTION using ONLY the z-conjunct.  Purely existential.

  CASE 1 (all colour 1). Needs a|x, a|y (drop the a^2-nondivisibility
        conjuncts: dropping them WEAKENS the hypothesis, so refuting the
        weaker version proves more).
        a|x and a|y => a | (x-y) = b t.  gcd(a,b)=1 (Bezout au+bv=1)
        => t = t(au+bv) = a(tu) + v(bt) => a | t => t = a*w, and
        1 <= a*w <= b < a  =>  0 < w < 1.  CONTRADICTION.
        gcd IS used here, via Bezout, which is EXISTENTIAL -- so it can be
        added as two extra free variables u,v in the refutation query.

  brute-force cross-check of the k=2 case analysis:
    k=2, all coprime b<a with 2<=a<=9: NO monochromatic solution. OK
